[{"source" ":org/Math-Academy" "forms" [[:db/retract 17592186385351 :answer-field/choices 17592186385352] [:db/retract 17592186385351 :answer-field/choices 17592186385353] [:db/retract 17592186385351 :answer-field/choices 17592186385354] [:db/retract 17592186385351 :answer-field/choices 17592186385355] [:db/retract 17592186385351 :answer-field/choices 17592186385356] [:db/retract 17592186124976 :question/answer-fields 17592186122456] {:db/id 17592186124438 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-ae3534f1-44d3-55be-bcdb-7634e16c97c5"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186124976 :question/worked-solution "The curve $C$ is the intersection of the surface $z=f(x,y)$ with the plane $y=1.$ Hence, the slope of the tangent to the curve at the point $P(1,1,0)$ will be given by the partial derivative $\\frac{∂z}{∂x}{|}_{(1,1)}.$\n\nTo get the slope, we evaluate the partial derivative $\\frac{∂z}{∂x}$ at $(1,1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂z}{∂x}{|}_{(1,1)} & =3(1)+6(1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1\\cdot 1) \\\\  & =3+6\\operatorname{ln}⁡1 \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the point-slope form of a straight line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z-z{|}_{(1,1)} & =\\frac{∂z}{∂x}{|}_{(1,1)}(x-1) \\\\ z-0 & =3(x-1) \\\\ z & =3x-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the tangent line to the curve $C$ at $P(1,1,0)$ can be given as the intersection of two planes, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}y=1 \\\\ z=3x-3\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186385351 :answer-field/correct "answer-940c73e1-fac8-5d96-a4d7-4f31a5f433a8" :answer-field/choices ["answer-1cd26c8b-fb1c-5766-9fbe-ab3b0f2403f4" "answer-9ab403d6-b2c8-5db7-ac14-47e28ec612f9" "answer-940c73e1-fac8-5d96-a4d7-4f31a5f433a8" "answer-3cbc826e-b561-565f-a693-c12cb77c5362" "answer-d540c582-ba40-5073-81c9-81443650b392"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1cd26c8b-fb1c-5766-9fbe-ab3b0f2403f4" :answer/id #uuid "1cd26c8b-fb1c-5766-9fbe-ab3b0f2403f4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}y=1 \\\\ z=2-2x\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9ab403d6-b2c8-5db7-ac14-47e28ec612f9" :answer/id #uuid "9ab403d6-b2c8-5db7-ac14-47e28ec612f9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}y=1 \\\\ z=2x-2\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-940c73e1-fac8-5d96-a4d7-4f31a5f433a8" :answer/id #uuid "940c73e1-fac8-5d96-a4d7-4f31a5f433a8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}y=1 \\\\ z=3x-3\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3cbc826e-b561-565f-a693-c12cb77c5362" :answer/id #uuid "3cbc826e-b561-565f-a693-c12cb77c5362" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}y=1 \\\\ z=3x\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d540c582-ba40-5073-81c9-81443650b392" :answer/id #uuid "d540c582-ba40-5073-81c9-81443650b392" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}y=1, \\\\ z=4x-4\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-ae3534f1-44d3-55be-bcdb-7634e16c97c5" :question/id #uuid "ae3534f1-44d3-55be-bcdb-7634e16c97c5" :question/math-academy-id "q-132594" :question/problem "The curve $C$ is the intersection of a surface $S,$ defined by $z=f(x,y),$ with the plane $y=\\pi .$ Given that the point $P(\\frac{1}{2},\\pi ,1)$ lies on $C$, and that ${f}_{x}=2x{e}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)$, find the equations of the tangent line to $C$ at $P.$" :question/worked-solution "The curve $C$ is the intersection of the surface $z=f(x,y)$ with the plane $y=\\pi .$ Hence, the slope of the tangent to the curve at the point $P(\\frac{1}{2},\\pi ,1)$ will be given by the partial derivative $\\frac{∂z}{∂x}{|}_{(1/2,\\pi )}.$\n\nTo get the slope, we evaluate the partial derivative $\\frac{∂z}{∂x}$ at $(\\frac{1}{2},\\pi ):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂z}{∂x}{|}_{(1/2,\\pi )} & =2(\\frac{1}{2}){e}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi /2)}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & ={e}^{0}+1 \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the point-slope form of a straight line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z-z{|}_{(1/2,\\pi )} & =\\frac{∂z}{∂x}{|}_{(1/2,\\pi )}(x-\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\ z-1 & =2(x-\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\ z & =2x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the tangent line to the curve $C$ at $P(\\frac{1}{2},\\pi ,1)$ can be given as the intersection of two planes, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}y=\\pi  \\\\ z=2x\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-37d670d1-3bff-5409-be4d-e79488473006"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-37d670d1-3bff-5409-be4d-e79488473006" :answer-field/id #uuid "37d670d1-3bff-5409-be4d-e79488473006" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-ef0b5a29-3a47-5678-8b2a-9278853cd35b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-becf689a-2251-5072-95a8-008d1c2e4200" "answer-ef0b5a29-3a47-5678-8b2a-9278853cd35b" "answer-10528982-819d-558d-b7b9-c606e71872b0" "answer-7d86ddc1-2c7d-548c-9b05-047b8457b098" "answer-a8e89105-6501-5255-9bbc-617aef43299e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-becf689a-2251-5072-95a8-008d1c2e4200" :answer/id #uuid "becf689a-2251-5072-95a8-008d1c2e4200" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}y=\\pi  \\\\ z=2x+\\pi \\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ef0b5a29-3a47-5678-8b2a-9278853cd35b" :answer/id #uuid "ef0b5a29-3a47-5678-8b2a-9278853cd35b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}y=\\pi  \\\\ z=2x\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-10528982-819d-558d-b7b9-c606e71872b0" :answer/id #uuid "10528982-819d-558d-b7b9-c606e71872b0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}y=\\pi  \\\\ z=3x+1\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7d86ddc1-2c7d-548c-9b05-047b8457b098" :answer/id #uuid "7d86ddc1-2c7d-548c-9b05-047b8457b098" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}y=\\pi  \\\\ z=x-1\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a8e89105-6501-5255-9bbc-617aef43299e" :answer/id #uuid "a8e89105-6501-5255-9bbc-617aef43299e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}y=\\pi  \\\\ z=x-\\pi \\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186268892 :question/worked-solution "The curve $C$ is the intersection of the surface with the plane $x=-2.$ Hence, the slope of the tangent to the curve $C$ at the point $P$ will be given by the partial derivative ${f}_{y}(-2,2).$ \n\nTo get the slope, we evaluate the partial derivative ${f}_{y}(x,y)$ at $(-2,2):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{y}(-2,2) & =(-2)^{2}(2)+2(-2)-(2) \\\\  & =8-4-2 \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we use the point-slope form of a straight line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z-f(-2,2) & ={f}_{y}(-2,2)(y-2) \\\\ z-3 & =2(y-2) \\\\ z & =2y-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the tangent line to the curve $C$ at $P(-2,2,3)$ can be given as the intersection of two planes:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=-2 \\\\ z=2y-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, notice that:\n\n- For the plane $x=-2,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨1,0,0⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $z=2y-1$ (or $2y-z-1=0$), a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨0,2,-1⟩.$\n\nFinally, to find a direction vector for the tangent line, we calculate the cross product of these normal vectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} & =⟨1,0,0⟩\\times ⟨0,2,-1⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =j+2\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a tangent vector to $C$ at $P$ is $j+2\\,k.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "activity-dee62c26-4f96-5315-9736-66f2027d8581" :activity/id #uuid "dee62c26-4f96-5315-9736-66f2027d8581" :activity/title "Geometric Interpretations of Partial Derivatives" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186050158 :activity/course 17592186046658 :activity/steps ["step-39707566-6312-542f-af0b-85f44247ceeb" "step-f46d0be1-bd90-5c9e-ab3f-e22acfe2493d" "step-b5bc4d9f-ec45-5df0-ba2f-64b35987a453" "step-1430ce69-365b-5d69-8d4b-3d05c2d08e10" "step-a34f7fed-6748-57b7-896d-3a0ab90523d6"] :activity/first-step "step-39707566-6312-542f-af0b-85f44247ceeb" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-39707566-6312-542f-af0b-85f44247ceeb" :step/id #uuid "39707566-6312-542f-af0b-85f44247ceeb" :step/content 17592186124976 :step/next "step-f46d0be1-bd90-5c9e-ab3f-e22acfe2493d" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-f46d0be1-bd90-5c9e-ab3f-e22acfe2493d" :step/id #uuid "f46d0be1-bd90-5c9e-ab3f-e22acfe2493d" :step/content 17592186500341 :step/next "step-b5bc4d9f-ec45-5df0-ba2f-64b35987a453" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-b5bc4d9f-ec45-5df0-ba2f-64b35987a453" :step/id #uuid "b5bc4d9f-ec45-5df0-ba2f-64b35987a453" :step/content 17592186425119 :step/next "step-1430ce69-365b-5d69-8d4b-3d05c2d08e10" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-1430ce69-365b-5d69-8d4b-3d05c2d08e10" :step/id #uuid "1430ce69-365b-5d69-8d4b-3d05c2d08e10" :step/content "question-ae3534f1-44d3-55be-bcdb-7634e16c97c5" :step/next "step-a34f7fed-6748-57b7-896d-3a0ab90523d6" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-a34f7fed-6748-57b7-896d-3a0ab90523d6" :step/id #uuid "a34f7fed-6748-57b7-896d-3a0ab90523d6" :step/content 17592186268892 :db/ensure [:step/validate]}] "assertions" [[17592186124976 :question/worked-solution "The curve $C$ is the intersection of the surface $z=f(x,y)$ with the plane $y=1.$ Hence, the slope of the tangent to the curve at the point $P(1,1,0)$ will be given by the partial derivative $\\frac{∂z}{∂x}{|}_{(1,1)}.$\n\nTo get the slope, we evaluate the partial derivative $\\frac{∂z}{∂x}$ at $(1,1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂z}{∂x}{|}_{(1,1)} & =3(1)+6(1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1\\cdot 1) \\\\  & =3+6\\operatorname{ln}⁡1 \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the point-slope form of a straight line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z-z{|}_{(1,1)} & =\\frac{∂z}{∂x}{|}_{(1,1)}(x-1) \\\\ z-0 & =3(x-1) \\\\ z & =3x-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the tangent line to the curve $C$ at $P(1,1,0)$ can be given as the intersection of two planes, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}y=1 \\\\ z=3x-3\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["answer-1cd26c8b-fb1c-5766-9fbe-ab3b0f2403f4" :answer/id #uuid "1cd26c8b-fb1c-5766-9fbe-ab3b0f2403f4"] ["answer-1cd26c8b-fb1c-5766-9fbe-ab3b0f2403f4" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-1cd26c8b-fb1c-5766-9fbe-ab3b0f2403f4" :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}y=1 \\\\ z=2-2x\\end{aligned}"] ["answer-9ab403d6-b2c8-5db7-ac14-47e28ec612f9" :answer/id #uuid "9ab403d6-b2c8-5db7-ac14-47e28ec612f9"] ["answer-9ab403d6-b2c8-5db7-ac14-47e28ec612f9" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-9ab403d6-b2c8-5db7-ac14-47e28ec612f9" :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}y=1 \\\\ z=2x-2\\end{aligned}"] ["answer-940c73e1-fac8-5d96-a4d7-4f31a5f433a8" :answer/id #uuid "940c73e1-fac8-5d96-a4d7-4f31a5f433a8"] ["answer-940c73e1-fac8-5d96-a4d7-4f31a5f433a8" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-940c73e1-fac8-5d96-a4d7-4f31a5f433a8" :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}y=1 \\\\ z=3x-3\\end{aligned}"] ["answer-3cbc826e-b561-565f-a693-c12cb77c5362" :answer/id #uuid "3cbc826e-b561-565f-a693-c12cb77c5362"] ["answer-3cbc826e-b561-565f-a693-c12cb77c5362" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-3cbc826e-b561-565f-a693-c12cb77c5362" :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}y=1 \\\\ z=3x\\end{aligned}"] ["answer-d540c582-ba40-5073-81c9-81443650b392" :answer/id #uuid "d540c582-ba40-5073-81c9-81443650b392"] ["answer-d540c582-ba40-5073-81c9-81443650b392" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-d540c582-ba40-5073-81c9-81443650b392" :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}y=1, \\\\ z=4x-4\\end{aligned}"] [17592186385351 :answer-field/correct "answer-940c73e1-fac8-5d96-a4d7-4f31a5f433a8"] [17592186385351 :answer-field/choices "answer-1cd26c8b-fb1c-5766-9