ion/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-37d670d1-3bff-5409-be4d-e79488473006" :answer-field/id #uuid "37d670d1-3bff-5409-be4d-e79488473006"] ["answer-becf689a-2251-5072-95a8-008d1c2e4200" :answer/id #uuid "becf689a-2251-5072-95a8-008d1c2e4200"] ["answer-becf689a-2251-5072-95a8-008d1c2e4200" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-becf689a-2251-5072-95a8-008d1c2e4200" :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}y=\\pi  \\\\ z=2x+\\pi \\end{aligned}"] ["answer-ef0b5a29-3a47-5678-8b2a-9278853cd35b" :answer/id #uuid "ef0b5a29-3a47-5678-8b2a-9278853cd35b"] ["answer-ef0b5a29-3a47-5678-8b2a-9278853cd35b" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-ef0b5a29-3a47-5678-8b2a-9278853cd35b" :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}y=\\pi  \\\\ z=2x\\end{aligned}"] ["answer-10528982-819d-558d-b7b9-c606e71872b0" :answer/id #uuid "10528982-819d-558d-b7b9-c606e71872b0"] ["answer-10528982-819d-558d-b7b9-c606e71872b0" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-10528982-819d-558d-b7b9-c606e71872b0" :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}y=\\pi  \\\\ z=3x+1\\end{aligned}"] ["answer-7d86ddc1-2c7d-548c-9b05-047b8457b098" :answer/id #uuid "7d86ddc1-2c7d-548c-9b05-047b8457b098"] ["answer-7d86ddc1-2c7d-548c-9b05-047b8457b098" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-7d86ddc1-2c7d-548c-9b05-047b8457b098" :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}y=\\pi  \\\\ z=x-1\\end{aligned}"] ["answer-a8e89105-6501-5255-9bbc-617aef43299e" :answer/id #uuid "a8e89105-6501-5255-9bbc-617aef43299e"] ["answer-a8e89105-6501-5255-9bbc-617aef43299e" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-a8e89105-6501-5255-9bbc-617aef43299e" :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}y=\\pi  \\\\ z=x-\\pi \\end{aligned}"] ["answer-field-37d670d1-3bff-5409-be4d-e79488473006" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-37d670d1-3bff-5409-be4d-e79488473006" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-37d670d1-3bff-5409-be4d-e79488473006" :answer-field/correct "answer-ef0b5a29-3a47-5678-8b2a-9278853cd35b"] ["answer-field-37d670d1-3bff-5409-be4d-e79488473006" :answer-field/choices "answer-becf689a-2251-5072-95a8-008d1c2e4200"] ["answer-field-37d670d1-3bff-5409-be4d-e79488473006" :answer-field/choices "answer-ef0b5a29-3a47-5678-8b2a-9278853cd35b"] ["answer-field-37d670d1-3bff-5409-be4d-e79488473006" :answer-field/choices "answer-10528982-819d-558d-b7b9-c606e71872b0"] ["answer-field-37d670d1-3bff-5409-be4d-e79488473006" :answer-field/choices "answer-7d86ddc1-2c7d-548c-9b05-047b8457b098"] ["answer-field-37d670d1-3bff-5409-be4d-e79488473006" :answer-field/choices "answer-a8e89105-6501-5255-9bbc-617aef43299e"] ["question-ae3534f1-44d3-55be-bcdb-7634e16c97c5" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-37d670d1-3bff-5409-be4d-e79488473006"] [17592186124438 :knowledge-point/questions "question-ae3534f1-44d3-55be-bcdb-7634e16c97c5"] [17592186268892 :question/worked-solution "The curve $C$ is the intersection of the surface with the plane $x=-2.$ Hence, the slope of the tangent to the curve $C$ at the point $P$ will be given by the partial derivative ${f}_{y}(-2,2).$ \n\nTo get the slope, we evaluate the partial derivative ${f}_{y}(x,y)$ at $(-2,2):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{y}(-2,2) & =(-2)^{2}(2)+2(-2)-(2) \\\\  & =8-4-2 \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we use the point-slope form of a straight line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z-f(-2,2) & ={f}_{y}(-2,2)(y-2) \\\\ z-3 & =2(y-2) \\\\ z & =2y-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the tangent line to the curve $C$ at $P(-2,2,3)$ can be given as the intersection of two planes:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=-2 \\\\ z=2y-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, notice that:\n\n- For the plane $x=-2,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨1,0,0⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $z=2y-1$ (or $2y-z-1=0$), a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨0,2,-1⟩.$\n\nFinally, to find a direction vector for the tangent line, we calculate the cross product of these normal vectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} & =⟨1,0,0⟩\\times ⟨0,2,-1⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =j+2\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a tangent vector to $C$ at $P$ is $j+2\\,k.$"] ["activity-dee62c26-4f96-5315-9736-66f2027d8581" :activity/id #uuid "dee62c26-4f96-5315-9736-66f2027d8581"] ["step-39707566-6312-542f-af0b-85f44247ceeb" :step/id #uuid "39707566-6312-542f-af0b-85f44247ceeb"] ["step-f46d0be1-bd90-5c9e-ab3f-e22acfe2493d" :step/id #uuid "f46d0be1-bd90-5c9e-ab3f-e22acfe2493d"] ["step-b5bc4d9f-ec45-5df0-ba2f-64b35987a453" :step/id #uuid "b5bc4d9f-ec45-5df0-ba2f-64b35987a453"] ["step-1430ce69-365b-5d69-8d4b-3d05c2d08e10" :step/id #uuid "1430ce69-365b-5d69-8d4b-3d05c2d08e10"] ["step-a34f7fed-6748-57b7-896d-3a0ab90523d6" :step/id #uuid "a34f7fed-6748-57b7-896d-3a0ab90523d6"] ["step-39707566-6312-542f-af0b-85f44247ceeb" :step/content 17592186124976] ["step-39707566-6312-542f-af0b-85f44247ceeb" :step/next "step-f46d0be1-bd90-5c9e-ab3f-e22acfe2493d"] ["step-f46d0be1-bd90-5c9e-ab3f-e22acfe2493d" :step/content 17592186500341] ["step-f46d0be1-bd90-5c9e-ab3f-e22acfe2493d" :step/next "step-b5bc4d9f-ec45-5df0-ba2f-64b35987a453"] ["step-b5bc4d9f-ec45-5df0-ba2f-64b35987a453" :step/content 17592186425119] ["step-b5bc4d9f-ec45-5df0-ba2f-64b35987a453" :step/next "step-1430ce69-365b-5d69-8d4b-3d05c2d08e10"] ["step-1430ce69-365b-5d69-8d4b-3d05c2d08e10" :step/content "question-ae3534f1-44d3-55be-bcdb-7634e16c97c5"] ["step-1430ce69-365b-5d69-8d4b-3d05c2d08e10" :step/next "step-a34f7fed-6748-57b7-896d-3a0ab90523d6"] ["step-a34f7fed-6748-57b7-896d-3a0ab90523d6" :step/content 17592186268892] ["activity-dee62c26-4f96-5315-9736-66f2027d8581" :activity/title "Geometric Interpretations of Partial Derivatives"] ["activity-dee62c26-4f96-5315-9736-66f2027d8581" :activity/type :activity.type/review] ["activity-dee62c26-4f96-5315-9736-66f2027d8581" :activity/scope 17592186050158] ["activity-dee62c26-4f96-5315-9736-66f2027d8581" :activity/course 17592186046658] ["activity-dee62c26-4f96-5315-9736-66f2027d8581" :activity/steps "step-39707566-6312-542f-af0b-85f44247ceeb"] ["activity-dee62c26-4f96-5315-9736-66f2027d8581" :activity/steps "step-f46d0be1-bd90-5c9e-ab3f-e22acfe2493d"] ["activity-dee62c26-4f96-5315-9736-66f2027d8581" :activity/steps "step-b5bc4d9f-ec45-5df0-ba2f-64b35987a453"] ["activity-dee62c26-4f96-5315-9736-66f2027d8581" :activity/steps "step-1430ce69-365b-5d69-8d4b-3d05c2d08e10"] ["activity-dee62c26-4f96-5315-9736-66f2027d8581" :activity/steps "step-a34f7fed-6748-57b7-896d-3a0ab90523d6"] ["activity-dee62c26-4f96-5315-9736-66f2027d8581" :activity/first-step "step-39707566-6312-542f-af0b-85f44247ceeb"]] "retractions" [[17592186124976 :question/worked-solution "The curve $C$ is the intersection of the surface $z=f(x,y)$ with the plane $y=1.$ Hence, the slope of the tangent to the curve at the point $P(1,1,0)$ will be given by the partial derivative $\\frac{∂z}{∂x}{|}_{(1,1)}.$\n\nTo get the slope, we evaluate the partial derivative $\\frac{∂z}{∂x}$ at $(1,1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂z}{∂x}{|}_{(1,1)} & =3(1)+6(1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1\\cdot 1) \\\\  & =3+6\\operatorname{ln}⁡1 \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the point-slope form of a straight line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z-z{|}_{(1,1)} & =\\frac{∂z}{∂x}{|}_{(1,1)}(x-1) \\\\ z-0 & =3(x-1) \\\\ z & =3x-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the tangent line to the curve $C$ at $P(1,1,0)$ can be given as the intersection of two planes, as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}y=1 \\\\ z=3x-3\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186385351 :answer-field/correct 17592186385355] [17592186385351 :answer-field/choices 17592186385352] [17592186385351 :answer-field/choices 17592186385353] [17592186385351 :answer-field/choices 17592186385354] [17592186385351 :answer-field/choices 17592186385355] [17592186385351 :answer-field/choices 17592186385356] [17592186124976 :question/answer-fields 17592186122456] [17592186268892 :question/worked-solution "The curve $C$ is the intersection of the surface with the plane $x=-2.$ Hence, the slope of the tangent to the curve $C$ at the point $P$ will be given by the partial derivative ${f}_{y}(-2,2).$ \n\nTo get the slope, we evaluate the partial derivative ${f}_{y}(x,y)$ at $(-2,2):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{y}(-2,2) & =(-2)^{2}(2)+2(-2)-(2) \\\\  & =8-4-2 \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we use the point-slope form of a straight line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z-f(-2,2) & ={f}_{y}(-2,2)(y-2) \\\\ z-3 & =2(y-2) \\\\ z & =2y-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the tangent line to the curve $C$ at $P(-2,2,3)$ can be given as the intersection of two planes:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=-2 \\\\ z=2y-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, notice that:\n\n- For the plane $x=-2,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨1,0,0⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $z=2y-1$ (or $2y-z-1=0$), a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨0,2,-1⟩.$\n\nFinally, to find a direction vector for the tangent line, we calculate the cross product of these normal vectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} & =⟨1,0,0⟩\\times ⟨0,2,-1⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =j+2\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a tangent vector to $C$ at $P$ is $j+2\\,k.$"]]}]